content.text:
The evidence points to one root cause: ts-travel-plan-service's outgoing seat-service calls had their request path rewritten. I'm not running more queries; the picture is consistent across the traces I checked.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "ts-travel-plan-service",
      "fault_kind": "http_response_body_corrupted",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT s.service_name callee, s.span_name, s.attr_http_response_status_code code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces s ON s.trace_id=c.trace_id AND s.parent_span_id=c.span_id WHERE c.service_name='ts-travel-plan-service' AND c.attr_span_kind='Client' AND s.service_name='ts-seat-service' GROUP BY 1,2,3",
          "claim": "In the incident, travel-plan's seat calls reached seat-service as 'POST /error' and got 403 (239 calls), not the normal left_tickets 200s."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT 'normal' p, s.span_name, s.attr_http_response_status_code code, count(*) n FROM normal_traces c JOIN normal_traces s ON s.trace_id=c.trace_id AND s.parent_span_id=c.span_id WHERE c.service_name='ts-travel-plan-service' AND c.attr_span_kind='Client' AND s.service_name='ts-seat-service' GROUP BY 1,2,3",
          "claim": "Normal period: travel-plan's calls to seat-service are POST /api/v1/seatservice/seats/left_tickets, all returning 200."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_status_code, attr_http_response_status_code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-travel-plan-service' AND attr_span_kind='Client' AND span_name='POST' GROUP BY 1,2,3",
          "claim": "Travel-plan's outgoing POST client spans carry 403 responses (239) in the incident window, with Error status."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_status_code, count(*) n, quantile_cont(duration,0.95)/1e6 p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-travel-plan-service' AND attr_span_kind='Server' GROUP BY 1,2 ORDER BY n DESC",
          "claim": "Travel-plan's own server spans for minStation and cheapest show Error status in the incident window."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "ts-travel-plan-service",
      "to": "ts-ui-dashboard",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT c.service_name caller, s.service_name callee, s.span_name, s.attr_status_code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces s ON s.trace_id=c.trace_id AND s.parent_span_id=c.span_id WHERE c.service_name='ts-ui-dashboard' AND s.service_name='ts-travel-plan-service' GROUP BY 1,2,3,4 ORDER BY n DESC",
          "claim": "ts-ui-dashboard's calls to travel-plan's minStation endpoint return Error status when travel-plan's server span errors, reaching the user-facing tier."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
